## Numbers, money and dates

`Number` and `DateTime` are not SDK enum values; the generator infers them from Java types (`Integer` / `Long`, `LocalDateTime`). They are shown here because ExUI renders them as distinct controls and this POC uses both on events.

**Date** and **DateTime** use ExUI’s `cut-date-input`: separate Day / Month / Year boxes. DateTime also shows Hour / Minute / Second. (If a field sets `dateTimeEntryFormat`, ExUI switches to a Material datetime picker instead — none of the TEC fields do.)

<div class="bf-elements">
<%= partial "partials/blockframe/element_tile", locals: { type: :money, name: "MoneyGBP" } %>
<%= partial "partials/blockframe/element_tile", locals: { type: :number, name: "Number", note: "Inferred from numeric Java types" } %>
<%= partial "partials/blockframe/element_tile", locals: { type: :date, name: "Date", note: "Day / Month / Year" } %>
<%= partial "partials/blockframe/element_tile", locals: { type: :datetime, name: "DateTime", note: "Day–Year + Hour / Minute / Second" } %>
</div>

